# issue #304 [E17.S3], .sdlc/plans/304.md Section 2/Step 7. The repo-root .gitignore already
# ignores node_modules/ and .next/ from insight/web/, but that file would not travel if insight/
# is ever extracted to its own repo -- this file keeps insight/web/'s own ignore rules inside the
# extractable tree.
#
# scripts/prove-metric-contract-safety.mjs's mkScratchInWeb() (Decision (b)) creates these,
# nested under insight/web/ itself so tsc's node_modules resolution finds the real
# @types/react -- torn down in a `finally` block on every run, so this is a defense against a
# crash mid-run leaving debris, not a correctness guard the test suite depends on.
.contract-proof-scratch-*/

# issue #307 [E18.S2], .sdlc/plans/307.md Task 4 -- found live during implementation:
# scripts/prove-python-bridge-exit-codes.mjs's fixture imports node:child_process/node:path, so
# its scratch compile needs tsc's ordinary upward node_modules walk to find @types/node, exactly
# the same reason .contract-proof-scratch-*/ exists above for @types/react. Torn down in a
# `finally` block on every run (runScenarioInWebAsync, tsc-scratch.mjs) -- not a correctness guard.
.python-bridge-proof-scratch-*/

# issue #307 [E18.S2] -- same reason again, one file over: the security review's fix gave
# secure.ts a `process.env` default, so its scratch compile now needs @types/node via tsc's
# upward node_modules walk, which only works rooted under insight/web/. Torn down in a `finally`.
.secure-cookie-proof-scratch-*/

# issue #308 [E18.S3], .sdlc/plans/308.md Task 4 -- same reason as the two entries above:
# prove-session-epoch-store.mjs's scratch compile needs @types/node too (sessionEpoch.ts imports
# node:crypto/node:fs/node:path). Torn down in a `finally` (runScenarioInWebAsync), not a
# correctness guard.
.session-epoch-proof-scratch-*/

# Not in the plan's file list -- added during implementation verification (Step 5's
# INSIGHT_DEV_ROUTES gate was probed locally via a throwaway .env.local, since this sandbox's
# Bash tool cannot pass ad hoc env vars or delete files it created). Standard Next.js convention;
# harmless to keep.
.env*.local
